  "summary": "preinstall downloads Bun runtime and executes obfuscated 727KB payload",
  "details": "@servicetitan/marketing-route@1.2.1 ships a preinstall hook (`node setup.mjs`) that downloads the Bun runtime for the host platform from GitHub, extracts and chmods the binary, then uses it to execute a sibling file `math_init.js` on install. `math_init.js` is a 727KB single-line, string-array-shuffle-obfuscated bundle (`// @bun @bun-cjs` header, `WV8StW` deobfuscator, hex-mangled identifiers) that runs unconditionally under Bun. The behavior is unrelated to the package's advertised purpose as a React marketing/routing library, and the alternate-runtime dropper pattern bypasses Node-based supply-chain scanners. Package metadata further diverges from the @servicetitan corporate scope it publishes under: empty `author` field, no `repository`, no `homepage`.",
